<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15</span></span><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;background:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Trigger Mechanism</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_para ltx_noindent" id="S4.SS2.p5">
<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data Collection.</span> Mycroft preallocates a fixed-size circular buffer in the host machine’s shared memory space during NCCL’s initialization stage. At each tracepoint, it acquires a pointer to the next available buffer slot and writes trace data directly into the memory space, minimizing the control loop overhead. This runs on NCCL’s internal streams to support asynchronous measurement, adding virtually no overhead to the critical path. A separate read-only agent consumes the data and uploads it to a cloud database via Kafka, avoiding locks and preventing back pressure. This design enables continuous runtime tracing with negligible overhead.</p>
</div>
<figure class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm" id="alg2">
<div class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_listing">
<div class="ltx_listingline">
